<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative results on AMBER benchmark for LLaVA-1.5-7B.<span id="S4.T2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We evaluate object hallucination using the AMBER benchmark under various mitigation methods, including combinations with our approach. AMBER measures hallucination in generative (Gen.) and discriminative (Disc.) settings, with its score offering a comprehensive assessment across both. The maximum token length is set to 512 for generative task. <math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>% denotes the relative difference in performance. </span></span></figcaption>
