<figure id="A7.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A7.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A8</span>: </span><span id="A7.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative results of our method on state-of-the-art LVLMs.<span id="A7.T8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We apply our approach to two SOTA models, DeepSeek-VL and Qwen2.5-VL, and compare performance against greedy decoding. For DeepSeek-VL we set <math id="A7.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{th}}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{th}}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, while for Qwen2.5-VL we use <math id="A7.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{th}}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{th}}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>. These results demonstrate that our method is applicable to a wide range of LVLMs, including the most recent architectures.</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="A7.T8.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.T8.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
